# OLD-PATH WARNINGS THE PROGRAM LAYER IS RIGHT NOT TO SAY, one per line, TAB-separated: the file
# under the repository (`*` for any), words the old path's message holds, and why it is no law. A
# warning is excused only where both its file and its words match; tools/witness_program_warnings.sh
# names each it excuses. A line no warning matches any longer is stale and is taken away.
*	— `shallow_at` writes through it	`shallow_at` folds the node it is handed and writes nothing through `self`
*	— `shallow_expr` writes through it	the generated arity fold reads the node it is handed and writes nothing through `self`
*	— `shallow_stmt` writes through it	the generated arity fold reads the node it is handed and writes nothing through `self`
*	— `param_fps` writes through it	`param_fps` reads each seat's identity and writes nothing through `self`
*	— `site_fingerprint` writes through it	`site_fingerprint` folds through `shallow_at` and writes nothing through `self`
packages/std-avrac/src/compiler/item_program.av	`w` is not `mut` — `layouts` writes through it	`layouts` builds a list of its fields and writes nothing through `self`
packages/std-avrac/src/compiler/workspace.av	`ws` is not `mut` — `arm_recording` writes through it	`arm_recording` writes only through `Cell`s, which every copy shares
